WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.720
[MUSIC]

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.198
In the summer of 1884,
four English sailors

00:00:14.198 --> 00:00:18.606
were stranded at sea in a
lifeboat in the south Atlantic,

00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:21.322
over 1,000 miles from land.

00:00:21.322 --> 00:00:26.243
Dudley was the captain, Stephens,
the first mate, and Brooks, a sailor.

00:00:26.263 --> 00:00:33.273
The fourth member of the crew was the
cabin boy, Richard Parker, age 17.

00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:36.002
The crew had few provisions.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:39.220
For the first three days,
they ate a can of turnips.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:44.600
On the fourth day, they caught a
turtle which sustained them for a time.

00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:49.049
But soon they had no food, amd
for eight days they ate nothing.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:54.869
By now, Parker-- the cabin boy--
was lying in the corner of the boat.

00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:58.821
He had drunk seawater and become ill.

00:00:58.821 --> 00:01:04.490
On the 19th day, Dudley-- the
captain-- suggested drawing lots

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:09.400
to determine who would die so
that the others might live.

00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:13.707
But Brooks refused,
and no lots were drawn.

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:18.135
The next day, Dudley decided
that Parker had to be killed.

00:01:18.135 --> 00:01:21.845
He offered a prayer, told
the boy his time had come,

00:01:21.845 --> 00:01:25.861
and killed him with a pen knife,
stabbing him in the jugular vein.

00:01:25.861 --> 00:01:30.658
For four days, the three
remaining crew members

00:01:30.658 --> 00:01:34.366
fed on the body and the
blood of the cabin boy.

00:01:34.366 --> 00:01:36.266
Then help came.

00:01:36.278 --> 00:01:40.398
On the 24th day, a ship
rescued the three survivors.

00:01:40.398 --> 00:01:44.644
Upon their return to England, they were
arrested and put on trial for murder.

00:01:44.644 --> 00:01:50.399
Dudley and Stephens confessed that
they had killed and eaten Parker,

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:55.259
but they claimed they had
done so out of necessity.

00:01:55.275 --> 00:01:58.025
Putting aside the question
of law, how do you

00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:01.099
judge the morality of what they did?

00:02:01.111 --> 00:02:05.468
Would you say they acted immorally
in killing and eating the cabin boy?

00:02:05.468 --> 00:02:09.693
Or would you say that,
all things considered,

00:02:09.693 --> 00:02:13.778
they did the right thing, sacrificing
one life in order to save three?

00:02:13.778 --> 00:02:20.568
[MUSIC]

